k;\">100%?</div></div></div>\n</div><div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-location\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Location\">Location</span></h3>\n<p>Under the Cemetery north of <a href=\"#/wiki/Edron\">Edron</a>.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-behaviour\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Behaviour\">Behaviour</span></h3>\n<p>\tCount Vlarkorth attacks in melee range. Count Vlarkorth never retreats.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-creature-strategy\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Strategy\">Strategy</span></h3>\n<p>\tUse Death Damage on the boss and <a href=\"#/wiki/Avalanche\">Avalanches</a> if you need to kill the summons. Make sure you keep the <a href=\"#/wiki/Soulless%20Minion\">Soulless Minions</a> away from the boss, otherwise it will heal too much and be very hard to kill. Twice during the fight, it will summon one <i>Dark &lt;vocation&gt;</i> for each player in the room. These must be killed and the respective vocation must use the corpse on Count Vlarkoth to make it vulnerable again. For example, a Druid must use the Good Remains of a Druid on the boss. <a href=\"#/wiki/Demon%20Skeleton\">Demon Skeletons</a> can be summoned in the room to help trap the boss, since its only magical attack deals <a href=\"#/wiki/Fire%20Damage\">Fire Damage</a>.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\">  <img alt=\"Grave_Danger_Quest_-_Count_Vlarkoth\" class=\"\" data-video-key=\"Grave_Danger_Quest_-_Count_Vlarkoth\" data-video-name=\"Grave Danger Quest - Count Vlarkoth\" height=\"168\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Grave_Danger_Quest_Count_Vlarkoth_ee6abe.png\" width=\"300\"/> <span class=\"thumbnail-play-icon-container\"> <svg aria-label=\"Play\" class=\"thumbnail-play-icon wds-icon\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-player-icon-play\"></use></svg> </span>  <figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<div>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Loot\">Loot</span></h3>\n<